            "id": "q_std1",
            "text": "First Impression of the community is within Atlas standard",
            "interpretive_guideline": "Upon arrival, Regional team members should assess both the exterior and interior environments with a focus on presentation, cleanliness, and overall upkeep.\n\nExterior / Curb Appeal\nThe landscaping and outward appearance of the community should align with Atlas standards. This includes well-maintained lawns, trimmed hedges, clean walkways, clear signage, and a welcoming, polished entrance. The exterior should convey pride, safety, and attention to detail, creating a positive and inviting first impression for residents, families, and visitors.\n\nInterior Environment\nUpon entering the community, the interior should be clean, well-lit, and in excellent repair. A key component of first impression is that the building is odor-free, with no noticeable or lingering unpleasant smells. Common areas, hallways, and resident-facing spaces should reflect consistent upkeep, organization, and a high standard of cleanliness. Furnishings, fixtures, and finishes should be in good condition, reinforcing a sense of quality and care. This also includes the full leadership team being dressed professionally and appropriately according to standards.",
